    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<b>Mature Themes</b><br><br>\n\nSynopsis: Eva is stuck in a world that keeps punching her down as she desperately tries to play the game: pay the bills, get him to football and survive the other mums' comments. On her way to an important job interview, intrusive thoughts take over. Guided by Arthur, a grotesque, sadistic half-real figure, Eva journeys through violent thoughts, trauma and self-hatred toward self-acceptance and empowerment. This new work comes fresh from success at the Edinburgh Festival.\n\n\n<style>\n\n@media screen and (max-width:728px) {\niframe{width:100%!important;}\n}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
