    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "An Evening with Kathleen Edwards"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p>After a powerful performance at the 30th anniversary of the Jubilee Music Festival, Kathleen Edwards returns to our indoor Main Stage for an unforgettable evening.</p><br>\n\n<p>Since her acclaimed 2002 debut, Failer, Edwards has built a remarkable career blending alt-country, folk and heartland rock. Her songwriting has earned more than half a dozen JUNO Award nominations and Top 40 success on both sides of the Canadian-American border.</p><br>\n\n<p>Over the past two decades, Edwards has released acclaimed albums including Back to Me, Asking for Flowers, Voyageur and Total Freedom. She has collaborated with artists such as Maren Morris and shared stages with Willie Nelson, John Fogerty and Bob Dylan.</p><br>\n\n<p>Known for her honest songwriting, ripping guitar riffs and great songs, Kathleen Edwards continues to connect with audiences while looking ahead to what comes next.</p><br>\n\n\n<style>\n.location-page-temp {display: block!important;}\n@media screen and (max-width: 600px){iframe{width:100%;}}\n</style>\n\n"
      }
